*GitHub Service:** Repository connection, file read/write, commits 3. **Project Service:** Project CRUD, metadata management 4. **Sync Service:** Bi-directional GitHub ↔ Supabase sync 5. **Rules Service:** 24 rules validation, auto-fix 6. **Notification Service:** Real-time notifications --- ## Database Design Philosophy **Hybrid Storage:** - **Source of Truth:** GitHub (markdown/YAML files) - **Cache Layer:** Supabase PostgreSQL (for fast queries, real-time) - **Sync Strategy:** Bi-directional with conflict resolution **Why Hybrid:** - Zero vendor lock-in (data in GitHub) - Fast queries (PostgreSQL indexes) - Real-time updates (Supabase Realtime) - Offline resilience (queue changes, sync later) **Key Principles:** - GitHub always wins conflicts - Supabase is read-optimized (denormalized where needed) - Periodic full re-sync from GitHub (integrity check) --- ## Security Model **Row-Level Security (RLS) in Supabase:** - Users see only their own projects - Collaborators have access based on GitHub repo permissions - Admin role for multi-user teams (future) **API Security:** - Supabase handles authentication - Next.js API routes validate sessions - GitHub tokens stored securely (Supabase vault or env) --- ## Real-time Updates **Supabase Realtime Channels:** - `project:{projectId}` - Project changes - `notifications:{userId}` - User notifications - `modules:{moduleId}` - Module status updates **Use Cases:** - Multi-user collaboration (see who's editing) - Live progress updates - Instant notifications --- ## Data Flow Examples **Example 1: User Updates PRD** ``` 1. User edits PRD form in React UI 2. React → Next.js API Route: PUT /api/projects/:id/prd 3. Next.js Service → Supabase: Update project table 4. Next.js Service → GitHub: Commit docs/core/01_PRD.md 5. Supabase Realtime → Other users: Notify of change ``` **Example 2: GitHub Webhook (file changed externally)** ``` 1. User edits markdown directly in GitHub 2. GitHub Webhook → Next.js API: POST /api/github/webhook 3. Next.js Service → Read changed file 4. Next.js Service → Supabase: Update project table 5. Supabase Realtime → All users: Notify of change ``` --- ## Scaling Considerations **Current (MVP):** - Single Supabase instance - Next.js on Vercel (auto-scaling) - GitHub API rate limits (5000 req/hour) **Future (v2.0+):** - Redis cache layer (reduce GitHub API calls) - Background jobs (Supabase Edge Functions) - Multi-region deployment (Vercel) - Database replicas (read scaling) --- ## Documentation References - [Entity Catalog](./entities/00_ENTITY_CATALOG.md) - [API Overview](./api/00_API_OVERVIEW.md) - [Services Catalog](./services/00_SERVICES_CATALOG.md) - [Database Schema](./database/00_DATABASE_SCHEMA.md) - [ADR Index](../adr/00_ADR_INDEX.md) --- **Next Steps:** 1. Design detailed entity schemas 2. Define API contracts (OpenAPI spec) 3. Set up Supabase project 4. Implement Row-Level Security policies 5. Create database migrations EOF echo "✅ Created 00_BACKEND_OVERVIEW.md"
