/:id/rules/fix` | Auto-fix violations | Required | --- ## Response Format **Success:** ```json { "success": true, "data": { ... } } ``` **Error:** ```json { "success": false, "error": { "code": "ERROR_CODE", "message": "Human-readable message" } } ``` --- ## Authentication All API routes check Supabase session: ```typescript const supabase = createServerClient(); const { data: { user } } = await supabase.auth.getUser(); if (!user) { return new Response('Unauthorized', { status: 401 }); } ``` --- ## Rate Limiting **Limits:** - Supabase: Built-in rate limiting - GitHub API: 5000 requests/hour per token **Strategy:** - Cache GitHub responses - Batch GitHub operations - Queue background syncs EOF cat > docs/backend/services/00_SERVICES_CATALOG.md << 'EOF' # Services Catalog **Last Updated:** 2025-11-14 **Total Services:** 6 core --- ## Core Services | Service | Purpose | Dependencies | Priority | |---------|---------|--------------|----------| | **Auth Service** | GitHub OAuth, sessions | Supabase Auth | CRITICAL | | **GitHub Service** | Repo connection, file I/O | GitHub API | CRITICAL | | **Project Service** | Project CRUD, metadata | Supabase | CRITICAL | | **Sync Service** | Bi-directional sync | GitHub, Supabase | CRITICAL | | **Rules Service** | 24 rules validation | Supabase | CRITICAL | | **Notification Service** | Real-time notifications | Supabase Realtime | IMPORTANT | --- ## Service Responsibilities ### Auth Service - GitHub OAuth flow - Session management - User profile sync ### GitHub Service - Repository connection validation - File read/write operations - Commit management - Branch operations - Conflict detection ### Project Service - Project CRUD operations - Metadata management - Completeness score calculation ### Sync Service - GitHub → Supabase sync - Supabase → GitHub sync - Conflict resolution (GitHub always wins) - Queue management for offline mode ### Rules Service - Validate 24 UPMT rules - Auto-fix simple violations - Generate completeness score ### Notification Service - Create notifications - Real-time push via Supabase - Notification preferences --- ## Service Architecture ``` ┌─────────────┐ │ UI Layer │ └──────┬──────┘ │ ┌──────▼──────────────┐ │ API Routes │ (Next.js) └──────┬──────────────┘ │ ┌──────▼──────────────┐ │ Services Layer │ (Business Logic) ├─────────────────────┤ │ - AuthService │ │ - GitHubService │ │ - ProjectService │ │ - SyncService │ │ - RulesService │ │ - NotificationSvc │ └──────┬──────────────┘ │ ┌──────▼──────────────┐ │ Repositories │ (Data Access) │ (Supabase Client) │ └─────────────────────┘ ``` --- ## Implementation Location ``` app/lib/services/ ├── auth.service.ts ├── github.service.ts ├── project.service.ts ├── sync.service.ts ├── rules.service.ts └── notification.service.ts ``` EOF cat > docs/backend/database/00_DATABASE_SCHEMA.md << 'EOF' # Database Schema **Database:** PostgreSQL 18.1 (Supabase) **Total Tables:** 10 core + 5 supporting --- ## Core Tables 1. **users** - User accounts (GitHub OAuth) 2. **projects** - UPMT projects 3. **repositories** - GitHub repo metadata 4. **modules** - Project modules 5. **functions** - Module functions 6. **sprints** - Agile sprints 7. **tasks** - Backlog tasks 8. **notifications** - Real-time notifications 9. **activities** - Activity timeline 10. **rule_violations** - Rule violations ## Supporting Tables 11. **sessions** - User sessions (Supabase Auth managed) 12. **webhook_events** - GitHub webhook history 13. **sync_logs** - Sync operation logs 14. **achievements** - Vibe Wizard achievements (v2.0) 15. **settings** - User preferences (v2.0) --- ## Schema Visualization See [relationships.md](./relationships.md) for ERD diagram. --- ## Migrations Strategy **Tool:** Supabase Migrations (SQL) **Location:** `supabase/migrations/` **Example Migration:** ```sql -- 20250114_initial_schema.sql CREATE TABLE users (...); CREATE TABLE projects (...); -- etc. ``` --- ## Indexes Strategy **Primary Indexes:** - All PKs are UUID with default index - All FKs have indexes for join performance **Performance Indexes:** - `projects.completeness_score` (dashboard queries) - `modules.status` (filtering) - `tasks.status` + `sprint_id` (Kanban board) --- ## RLS Policies Row-Level Security enabled on all tables: ```sql -- Example: Projects ALTER TABLE projects ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY; CREATE POLICY projects_select_own ON projects FOR SELECT USING (user_id = auth.uid()); ``` --- ## Backup Strategy **Supabase Automated Backups:** - Daily snapshots (7-day retention) - Point-in-time recovery **Manual Backups:** - Export critical data to GitHub (markdown/YAML) - Weekly full DB dumps for disaster recovery EOF cat > docs/backend/database/relationships.md << 'EOF' # Database Relationships **ERD:** Entity-Relationship Diagram --- ## Core Relationships ``` ┌──────────┐ │ user │ └─────┬────┘ │ 1 │ │ n ┌─────▼──────┐ ┌──────────────┐ │ project │ 1──1 │ repository │ └─────┬──────┘ └──────────────┘ │ 1 │ ├─────n─────┐ │ │ │ n │ n ┌─────▼────┐ ┌────▼──────┐ │ module │ │ sprint │ └─────┬────┘ └────┬──────┘ │ 1 │ 1 │ │ │ n │ n ┌─────▼────────┐ ┌▼──────┐ │ function │ │ task │ └──────────────┘ └───────┘ ``` --- ## Relationship Matrix | Parent | Child | Cardinality | Delete Cascade | |--------|-------|-------------|----------------| | user | project | 1:n | Yes | | project | repository | 1:1 | No | | project | module | 1:n | Yes | | module | function | 1:n | Yes | | project | sprint | 1:n | Yes | | sprint | task | 1:n | Yes | | user | notification | 1:n | Yes | | project | activity | 1:n | Yes | --- ## Foreign Key Constraints ```sql -- Project → User ALTER TABLE projects ADD CONSTRAINT fk_projects_user FOREIGN KEY (user_id) REFERENCES users(id) ON DELETE CASCADE; -- Module → Project ALTER TABLE modules ADD CONSTRAINT fk_modules_project FOREIGN KEY (project_id) REFERENCES projects(id) ON DELETE CASCADE; -- Function → Module ALTER TABLE functions ADD CONSTRAINT fk_functions_module FOREIGN KEY (module_id) REFERENCES modules(id) ON DEL